{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1257757-silly-crossover-idea-gems-in-owod","id":1257757,"title":"Silly crossover idea: Gems in oWoD","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-09-28T05:52:29-07:00","id":1257757,"title":"Silly crossover idea: Gems in oWoD","content":"So I've been a fan of this silly cartoon for a while called Steven Universe. Despite being for children, I think the series has enough grit for its gem species to fit into WoD.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://steven-universe.wikia.com/wiki/Gems\" target=\"_blank\">Wikia link to the species info.</a><br /> <br /> I think they might function similar to inanimae, in that their gems are their anchors.<br /> <br /> Any ideas? I admit I am pretty bad at mechanical stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-29T11:16:56-07:00","id":1258000,"title":"","content":"Perhaps take a page from Lost in how it modifies its basic, broad splats? Otherwise, you'd never manage to fit all the potential gems in existence into a comfortably-sized splat section, especially with the ongoing discovery and description of more mineral species.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-29T11:32:01-07:00","id":1258001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1257757-silly-crossover-idea-gems-in-owod?p=1258000#post1258000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps take a page from Lost in how it modifies its basic, broad splats? Otherwise, you'd never manage to fit all the potential gems in existence into a comfortably-sized splat section, especially with the ongoing discovery and description of more mineral species.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, for sure. Luckily there ARE some defined gem roles that can serve as 'seemings.' Given the nature of the gem species, they'd be the best in Changeling games, with Werewolf as a second option.<br /> <br /> Quartzes are the space marines of the species, tough and fearless. Rubies are cannon fodder, while Sapphires are ironically aristocrats and seers.<br /> <br /> The Diamonds are just plain True Fae lite, given their abilities and size.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom